{"title":"Career Roadmap · Lab Technologist","role":"Lab Technologist","summary":"A Lab Technologist with a Genetics background works in laboratory environments performing sample preparation, molecular testing, DNA/RNA analysis, PCR, electrophoresis, genotyping, quality control and laboratory documentation. Depending on the workplace, the role can span research, biotechnology, molecular diagnostics, pharmaceutical R&D, agriculture and genetic testing.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc. (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Genetics"},"about":[{"label":"Career reality","text":"A B.Sc. can support entry-level laboratory roles, but many advanced molecular biology, clinical-genetics and research positions prefer or require an M.Sc./M.Tech./M.Phil./Ph.D. or relevant professional qualification. Clinical diagnostic roles may also have specific regulatory and employer requirements."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2027"},{"text":"Cell biology, genetics, biochemistry and laboratory fundamentals"}],[{"text":"2027–2028"},{"text":"Molecular biology, microbiology and core laboratory techniques"}],[{"text":"2028–2029"},{"text":"PCR, electrophoresis, DNA/RNA workflows and laboratory internship"}],[{"text":"2029–2030"},{"text":"Entry-level laboratory/biotech role or M.Sc."}],[{"text":"2030–2034"},{"text":"Molecular testing, research and quality systems"}],[{"text":"2034–2038"},{"text":"Senior Lab Technologist / Molecular Biology Specialist"}],[{"text":"2038–2042"},{"text":"Laboratory Supervisor / Technical Specialist"}],[{"text":"2042–2046"},{"text":"Lab Manager / Technical Lead / Research Specialist"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Key Skills","Proof"],"rows":[[{"text":"1st Year"},{"text":"Life-science foundation"},{"text":"Cell biology, genetics, bi